  "question": {
    "text": "The line $A B$ cuts off equal intercepts $2 a$ from the axes. From any point $P$ on the line $A B$ perpendiculars $P R$ and $P S$ are drawn on the axes. Locus of mid-point of $R S$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "PYuPz",
      "text": "$x-y=\\frac{a}{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "XRGn8",
      "text": "$x+y=a$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "nzHNk",
      "text": "$x^{2}+y^{2}=4 a^{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "owIo8",
      "text": "$x^{2}-y^{2}=2 a^{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\Rightarrow$\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\\frac{x}{2 a}+\\frac{y}{2 a}=1 \\\\\r\nx+y=2 a\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2016_mat_a32.png\">\r\n\r\nLet the coordinates of the mid-point of $\\mathrm{RS}$ be $(\\mathrm{h}, \\mathrm{k})$\r\nSo. $R$ and $S$ are $(2 h, 0)$ and $(0,2 k)$ Hence, the mid-point of $R S$ is $(h, k)$\r\nP lies on line AB\r\nThen. from Eq  we have\r\n$$\r\n2 h+2 k=2 a\r\n$$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad h+k=a$\r\nSo, the locus of $(h, k)$ is $x+y=a$.",
    "image": null
  },
